# Dialect-phase chunk output: derived from a source whose rights are not yet cleared
# (license: unverified_pending_review).
#
# THIS PATH MUST NEVER BECOME TRACKED. Git stops applying ignore rules to a path once
# it is tracked, so a single commit of this filename silently disables the only
# control holding back 337 dialect chunks - and the licence audit cannot catch it,
# because the audit compares AGAINST this corpus and cannot flag it as a leak of
# itself. It happened on 2026-09-09: a teammate ran chunk.py without --out, whose
# default is exactly this path, and pushed the result. Verified at the time:
# check-ignore reported NOT IGNORED and `git add -A` would have staged the held
# corpus. Fixed by renaming that file to data/processed/chunks_combined.jsonl.
#
# Per-source outputs belong at data/processed/chunks_<source>.jsonl. The unsuffixed
# name is the dialect phase's, and it is load-bearing for containment.
data/processed/chunks.jsonl

# Local-only EDA build that reproduces source excerpts (see eda.py --no-examples)
data/eda/*_with_examples.md

# Residue review log: its context column quotes readable source text
docs/residue_tokens_review.csv

# Task 3 fact-reference tables and review queues for the DIALECT corpus. Every `value`
# field, and the review CSV's `context` column, is a verbatim span lifted out of
# chunks.jsonl - so these carry the same rights status as the dialect source text
# itself and are held back for exactly as long as the corpus commit is held (see
# docs/SESSION_HANDOFF.md, hard rule in section 1).
#
# The classical corpus's equivalents are deliberately NOT ignored: that corpus is
# CC BY-SA with attribution recorded in the manifest, and it is already public.
data/processed/facts_saudi_dialect.jsonl
docs/citation_review_saudi_dialect.csv

# Task 3 fact-checker fixtures for the DIALECT corpus. The synthetic candidate
# responses quote dialect headwords and poet names taken from real chunks, so they
# carry the same rights status as the corpus. The classical fixture
# (tests/fixtures/candidates_classical_lexicon.jsonl) is CC BY-SA and is NOT ignored.
tests/fixtures/*saudi_dialect*

# LLM judge transcripts (Task 3, Group B). Added BEFORE any transcript exists, because
# the first real judge run is the moment the risk appears and a rule added afterwards is
# a rule added too late.
#
# judge_client.CachingBackend records the full prompt of every call so a paid run can be
# replayed offline for free. A judge prompt EMBEDS THE ENTIRE SOURCE CHUNK - see
# judge_sft.USER_TEMPLATE and judge_dpo.USER_TEMPLATE - so a transcript over dialect
# probes contains verbatim rights-pending source text, and inherits its status exactly
# like facts_saudi_dialect.jsonl above. A classical-only transcript would be CC BY-SA and
# safe, but the two are indistinguishable by filename, and getting that judgement wrong
# once publishes the corpus. Ignore all of them.
#
# سجلّات الحَكَم تتضمّن نص المصدر كاملًا، فترث حالة الحقوق نفسها.
#
# The pattern is deliberately broad and case-folded. It covers rotation and splitting by
# date or run id (judge_transcript_2026-09-05.jsonl, judge_transcript_run42.jsonl,
# .jsonl.1, .gz), the hyphen spelling, a judge_transcripts/ directory and everything
# under it, and any directory - not just data/. Case-folding is not paranoia: this repo
# has already shipped one ignore rule (docs/*handoff*.md) that worked only because
# Windows sets core.ignorecase, and would have missed a mixed-case file on a teammate's
# Linux clone. Verified against a simulated case-sensitive clone: 14 transcript spellings
# ignored, and the committed judge modules, fixtures and docs all still tracked.
*[Jj][Uu][Dd][Gg][Ee]*[Tt][Rr][Aa][Nn][Ss][Cc][Rr][Ii][Pp][Tt]*

# Session handoff notes: local continuity between working sessions. NEVER committed.
# They carry in-progress context, unreleased decisions and rights questions still open,
# and a local-only commit could be swept into a future push by accident. Keeping them
# out of git entirely is the stronger guarantee. They persist on disk; they never enter
# history. Pattern covers any future handoff file, not just the current one.
#
# Case-folded by hand. This previously read as two patterns, *HANDOFF* and *handoff*,
# which covered the all-caps and all-lower spellings but not a mixed-case one such as
# Session_Handoff.md. On Windows core.ignorecase hides that; on a case-sensitive clone
# it does not, so a teammate's mixed-case handoff would have shown up as a normal
# untracked file. The pre-commit audit would not catch it either: a handoff is prose
# ABOUT the corpus, not verbatim source text, so it passes an audit built to find
# quoted Arabic. One bracket pattern covers every spelling.
docs/*[Hh][Aa][Nn][Dd][Oo][Ff][Ff]*.md

# Adapter output: locked-schema records rebuilt from Task 2's generated files by
# src/verification/adapt_task2.py. Regenerable in one command, so committing it would
# only create a copy that can drift from its source. Classical-derived, so there is no
# rights question here - this is a staleness rule, not a containment one.
#
# NOTE: if the adapter is ever run over DIALECT records, its output inherits the
# rights-pending status of the corpus and this rule is then load-bearing for
# containment as well.
data/adapted/

# THE SAME CONDITIONAL APPLIES TO THE GROUP D REPORTS, and is written here because the
# files are TRACKED and therefore easy to forget about:
#   data/processed/duplication_report.json
#   data/processed/leakage_report.json
# check_duplication.py embeds up to 120 characters of record text per finding so that a
# reviewer can judge a flagged duplicate without opening the data. Today every adapted
# record is classical-derived (asas_albalagha, CC BY-SA) and Task 2's generated files are
# themselves tracked, so those excerpts add no exposure and the audit passes them clean.
# If either checker is ever run over DIALECT-derived records, its report inherits the
# rights-pending status of that corpus and MUST be moved behind an ignore rule in the
# same change - a tracked path is exactly how the chunks.jsonl regression happened.
# The licence audit is the backstop: it reads the staged report and refuses HELD_ONLY
# text. Do not rely on it alone.
